      "writtenOn": "2024-12-02T06:19:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Can we pass the request to enableIpServing as well? It has useful information in it, such as the connectivity scope, and in the future, the interface name. Right now your code calls enableIpServing -\u003e ensureIpServerStarted and creates the IpServer, but doesn\u0027t put the TetheringRequest in, then it calls tether, which then tries to figure out what request it was supposed to serve and notifies the IpServer of it.\n\nSome tethering types (like wifi, on new releases) will pass the TetheringRequest back to us. But even for those that don\u0027t, it would be better to determine the TetheringRequest that is being served as soon as possible instead of guessing it later.",
